#== News

== About me
I am a PhD student in the [https://math.ucsd.edu/ Department of Mathematics] at UC San Diego. I am very fortunate to be advised by 
[https://math.ucsd.edu/people/profiles/ioana-dumitriu Ioana Dumitriu] and [https://mathweb.ucsd.edu/~tkemp/ Todd Kemp]. I interned during Summer 2021 and 2022 with [https://www.pnnl.gov/people/tony-chiang Tony Chiang] at Pacific Northwest National Laboratory.
Prior to UCSD, I received my M.Sc. degree in Mathematics from Texas A&M University, supervised by [https://www.math.tamu.edu/~manshel/ Michael Anshelevich], and my B.Sc. degree in Mathematics and Applied Math from Chinese Academy of Sciences Hua Loo-Keng Class at [https://ev.buaa.edu.cn/ Beihang University].

#== Education 

== Research Interests
My current research focuses on theoretically understanding and improving fundamental algorithms in data science, especially in deep learning, using tools from high-dimensional probability. \n
- Random Matrix Theory and Free Probability Theory
- Deep Learning Theory and Foundations of AI
- High-dimensional Statistics

